    "durationMs": 319281,
    "finalText": "Implementation complete. Here's what I built and verified:\n\n**Files**\n- `src/main.rs` — Axum 0.8.4 app with sqlx (PostgreSQL) as the persistence layer; reads `DATABASE_URL`, retries briefly if the DB is still starting, applies embedded migrations, then serves on `0.0.0.0:8000`\n- `migrations/0001_create_links.sql` — `links` table (`code` unique, `url`, `clicks`, creation ordering by `id`)\n- `start.sh` (executable) — checks `DATABASE_URL`, builds the release binary only if missing (already prebuilt, so it starts instantly), runs migrations, serves in the foreground\n- `README.md` — startup instructions and API summary\n\n**Design points**\n- POST bodies are parsed from raw bytes with serde so malformed JSON, missing/invalid `url`, and invalid codes all return **422** with an `{\"error\"}` field (axum's `Json` extractor would have returned 400 for syntax errors)\n- Redirect uses a single atomic `UPDATE ... SET clicks = clicks + 1 ... RETURNING url` — exactly one increment per request, 302 with `Location` equal to the stored URL verbatim\n- Duplicate custom code → **409** (unique-violation detection); generated codes retry on the astronomically rare collision\n- Invalid-format codes on any endpoint → 422; valid-format unknown codes → 404\n\n**Verified end-to-end**: create (auto + custom codes, submitted URL returned unchanged), duplicate → 409, all 422 validation cases (bad URLs, missing url, malformed JSON, short/long/special-char codes), 404s, list ordering, 20 concurrent redirects incrementing clicks by exactly 20, and full data persistence across a server restart. Test data was wiped and the server stopped, so the suite starts clean; `sh start.sh` brings it up."
